    {
      "evidence_id": "tei:abstract",
      "source": "grobid_tei",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "We specify OCH, the first authenticated encryption with associated data scheme built to provide 128-bit multiuser AE security, 128-bit context commitment security, and 256-bit nonces with optional nonce privacy. It therefore addresses pressing limitations of currently widely-deployed schemes. We construct and formally analyze the security of OCH in a modular fashion, with transforms that are of broader applicability. On Intel Raptor Lake CPUs, OCH using the Areion permutation family has a peak encryption speed of 0.62 cycles per byte (cpb), not far off from AES128-GCM (0.38cpb) and outperforming both ChaCha20/Poly1305 (1.63cpb) and TurboSHAKE128-Wrap (3.52cpb). CCS Concepts • Security and privacy → Symmetric cryptography and hash functions; Mathematical foundations of cryptography."
    },
